
<section class="faq-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="faq-categories stagger">
      <button class="faq-cat-btn is-active" data-category="all">All questions</button>
      <button class="faq-cat-btn" data-category="orders">Orders</button>
      <button class="faq-cat-btn" data-category="shipping">Shipping</button>
      <button class="faq-cat-btn" data-category="products">Products</button>
      <button class="faq-cat-btn" data-category="care">Candle care</button>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-list stagger">
      <details class="faq-item reveal" data-category="orders">
        <summary>How do I track my order?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">Once your order ships, you'll receive an email with a tracking number. You can also view tracking anytime in your account under "Order history." Most orders ship within 1–2 business days.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item reveal" data-category="orders">
        <summary>Can I modify or cancel my order?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">We process orders quickly, but if you need to make a change, please email us at hello@auraandoak.com within 2 hours of placing your order. After that, we may not be able to accommodate changes.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item reveal" data-category="shipping">
        <summary>How long does shipping take?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">Standard shipping (3–5 business days) is complimentary on orders over $75. Expedited shipping (1–2 business days) is available at checkout. We ship from Portland, OR.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item reveal" data-category="shipping">
        <summary>Do you ship internationally?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">Yes, we ship to most countries. International shipping rates and delivery times vary. Please note that customers are responsible for any customs duties or import taxes.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item reveal" data-category="shipping">
        <summary>What's your return policy?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">We accept returns within 30 days of delivery on unopened items. If your candle arrives damaged, please email us within 7 days with photos and we'll replace it immediately. Opened candles cannot be returned for hygiene reasons, but we stand behind our products — reach out if there's an issue.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item reveal" data-category="products">
        <summary>Are your candles phthalate-free?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">Yes. Every fragrance we use is free of phthalates, parabens, and synthetic musks. We work only with independent perfumers who meet our strict safety and sustainability standards.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item reveal" data-category="products">
        <summary>What kind of wax do you use?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">100% American-grown soy wax. It's renewable, biodegradable, and burns cleaner than paraffin — no petroleum byproducts, no black soot on your walls.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item reveal" data-category="products">
        <summary>How long do your candles burn?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">Our 8 oz candles burn for approximately 45–50 hours. Our 13 oz candles burn for approximately 75–80 hours. Actual burn time depends on how you care for the candle.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item reveal" data-category="care">
        <summary>How do I prevent my candle from tunneling?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">On the first burn, let the wax pool reach the edge of the vessel (about 2 hours for the 8 oz, 3 hours for the 13 oz). This creates a "memory" that prevents tunneling on future burns. Always trim the wick to 1/4 inch before relighting.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item reveal" data-category="care">
        <summary>Can I refill my vessel?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">Yes! We offer a refill program. Send back your clean, empty vessel and we'll refill it for 30% off. Or bring it to our Portland studio. You can also clean it yourself and use it as a cup, planter, or catch-all.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item reveal" data-category="care">
        <summary>How do I clean candle wax from my vessel?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">Place the vessel in the freezer for 30 minutes. The wax will contract and pop out easily. Wipe the inside with a paper towel, then wash with warm soapy water. Don't pour wax down the drain.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item reveal" data-category="products">
        <summary>Are your products safe for pets?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">Our soy wax and cotton wicks are non-toxic. However, some essential oils can be irritating to pets, particularly cats. We recommend keeping lit candles away from pets and ensuring good ventilation. If you have concerns, consult your veterinarian.</div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

